From 8ef5b3dcc07ce1165b6474a0b86e05bd2840e81b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:07:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mt76: mt7915: unblock TX queues after the token reinit
 on reset

When the token pool hits token_size - MT76_TOKEN_FREE_THR,
mt76_token_consume() sets q->blocked on the band rings. The block is
cleared only from the TX free path: mt76_token_release() reports a wake
and mt7915_mac_tx_free_done() calls mt76_set_tx_blocked(false).

If SER or a full restart starts while the pool is blocked,
mt76_connac2_tx_token_put() frees every token but leaves q->blocked set.
After the reset no token is in flight, so no TX free event comes. On
mt7915 the PSD/ALTX queue shares the blocked ring
(mt76_connac_init_tx_queues()), so the pending and TXQ schedulers send
no frame at all, not even a management frame, that could take a token
and give it back. TX then stays stopped until some unrelated TX free
event reports a wake. A later reset does not help, because it also
leaves q->blocked set.

Clear the block right after the token idr is set up again, in both
mt7915_mac_restart() and the L1 SER path of mt7915_mac_reset_work().
The TX worker is still disabled at that point and is enabled at the end
of the reset, as before.
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index ee5f7814..78bad7bd 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1347,6 +1347,7 @@ mt7915_mac_restart(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 	/* token reinit */
 	mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(&dev->mt76);
 	idr_init(&dev->mt76.token);
+	mt76_set_tx_blocked(&dev->mt76, false);
 
 	mt7915_dma_reset(dev, true);
 
@@ -1564,6 +1565,7 @@ void mt7915_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 		mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(&dev->mt76);
 		idr_init(&dev->mt76.token);
+		mt76_set_tx_blocked(&dev->mt76, false);
 
 		mt76_wr(dev, MT_MCU_INT_EVENT, MT_MCU_INT_EVENT_DMA_INIT);
 		mt7915_wait_reset_state(dev, MT_MCU_CMD_RECOVERY_DONE);
-- 
